// Generalization of issue #350/#388's fix: a self-recursive local `fun`
// AND a second local `fun` that captures an ordinary local, both declared
// (and both captured) inside the SAME try block. The catch clause's own
// `e` binding reuses `x`'s slot (the first of the three top-level try
// locals to be freed) -- isFreshDeclaration (jvm_emitter.cpp) must still
// recognize it as a fresh declaration and route it to a plain store, not
// just for the single-capture shape either original issue named alone.
// Confirmed: this program hits the original "VerifyError: Register N
// contains wrong type" when isFreshDeclaration is disabled.

var fns = [];
try {
    var x = 10;
    fun f() { return f; }
    fun g() { return x; }
    fns.append(f);
    fns.append(g);
} catch (e) { print e; }
print fns[1]();

// CHECK: 10
